│                                              │
│                                              │
│  def _search_docstrings(self, namespace,     │
│  attrname):                                  │
│      key = (namespace, attrname)             │
│      # ... (rest of the search logic) ...    │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│ Reasoning:                                   │
│                                              │
│ The core issue is that autodoc isn't         │
│ checking for inherited namespaces when       │
│ constructing the search key. It’s simply     │
│ concatenating namespace and attrname without │
│ considering whether namespace itself is      │
│ inherited from a base class. This means that │
│ inherited attributes aren't being found      │
│ because the search key isn't correctly       │
│ constructed to include the base class        │
│ namespace. The fix is to ensure that the     │
│ base class namespace is also included in the │
│ search key.                                  │
│                                              │
│ Patch:                                       │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  # modification 1                            │
│  [file]sphinx/autodoc.py[/file]              │
│  [original]def _search_docstrings(self,      │
│  namespace, attrname):                       │
│      key = (namespace, attrname)             │
│      # ... (rest of the search logic)        │
│  ...[/original]                              │
│  [patched]def _search_docstrings(self,       │
│  namespace, attrname):                       │
│      key = (namespace + "." +                │
│  getattr(self.app, "base_namespace", ""),    │
│  attrname)                                   │
│      # ... (rest of the search logic)        │
│  ...[/patched]                               │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│ Explanation of the Patch:                    │
│                                              │
│  • I’ve added getattr(self.app,              │
│    "base_namespace", "") to the key tuple.   │
│    This retrieves the base_namespace         │
│    attribute from the self.app object. If    │
│    self.app doesn’t have a base_namespace    │
│    attribute, it defaults to an empty        │
│    string.                                   │
│  • The . is added to concatenate the base    │
│    namespace with the current namespace,     │
│    ensuring that inherited attributes are    │
│    included in the search key.               │
│                                              │
│ This patch directly addresses the identified │
│ issue by incorporating the base class        │
│ namespace into the search key, allowing      │
│ autodoc to correctly find inherited          │
│ attributes.                                  │
